# CRUD Back-Office — Convention du projet

Quand une nouvelle table est créée, générer systématiquement les **7 artefacts** suivants.

## Architecture générale

```
Controller  →  UseCase  →  Repository (interface)  →  EloquentRepository
```

- **Controller** : valide la requête HTTP, délègue au Use Case, retourne la réponse.
- **UseCase** (`app/UseCases/{Resource}/`) : logique métier, réutilisable partout dans le backend.
- **Repository interface** (`app/Contracts/Repositories/`) : contrat d'accès aux données.
- **Eloquent Repository** (`app/Repositories/`) : implémentation concrète via Eloquent.
- Le binding interface → implémentation se fait dans `AppServiceProvider::register()`.

---

## 1. Routes (`routes/web.php`)

Ajouter un groupe dans le bloc admin existant :

```php
Route::middleware('right:admin.{resources}')->group(function () {
    Route::get('/{resources}', [{Resource}ManagementController::class, 'index'])->name('{resources}.index');
    Route::post('/{resources}', [{Resource}ManagementController::class, 'store'])->name('{resources}.store');
    Route::put('/{resources}/{{resource}}', [{Resource}ManagementController::class, 'update'])->name('{resources}.update');
    Route::delete('/{resources}/{{resource}}', [{Resource}ManagementController::class, 'destroy'])->name('{resources}.destroy');
});
```

---

## 2. Repository interface (`app/Contracts/Repositories/{Resource}RepositoryInterface.php`)

```php
namespace App\Contracts\Repositories;

use App\Models\{Resource};
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Collection;

interface {Resource}RepositoryInterface
{
    public function findById(string $id): ?{Resource};
    /** @return Collection<int, {Resource}> */
    public function all(): Collection;
    /** @param array<string, mixed> $data */
    public function create(array $data): {Resource};
    /** @param array<string, mixed> $data */
    public function update({Resource} ${resource}, array $data): {Resource};
    public function delete({Resource} ${resource}): bool;
}
```

---

## 3. Eloquent Repository (`app/Repositories/Eloquent{Resource}Repository.php`)

```php
namespace App\Repositories;

use App\Contracts\Repositories\{Resource}RepositoryInterface;
use App\Models\{Resource};
use Illuminate\Database\Eloquent\Collection;

class Eloquent{Resource}Repository implements {Resource}RepositoryInterface
{
    public function findById(string $id): ?{Resource} { return {Resource}::find($id); }

    public function all(): Collection
    {
        return {Resource}::query()->orderBy('name')->get();
    }

    public function create(array $data): {Resource} { return {Resource}::create($data); }

    public function update({Resource} ${resource}, array $data): {Resource}
    {
        ${resource}->update($data);
        return ${resource}->fresh() ?? ${resource};
    }

    public function delete({Resource} ${resource}): bool { return (bool) ${resource}->delete(); }
}
```

Puis ajouter dans `AppServiceProvider::register()` :

```php
$this->app->bind({Resource}RepositoryInterface::class, Eloquent{Resource}Repository::class);
```

---

## 4. Use Cases (`app/UseCases/{Resource}/`)

Créer un fichier par action. Exemple complet pour `Create` :

```php
namespace App\UseCases\{Resource};

use App\Contracts\Repositories\{Resource}RepositoryInterface;
use App\Models\{Resource};

class Create{Resource}UseCase
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly {Resource}RepositoryInterface ${resources},
    ) {}

    public function execute(string $name /* … autres paramètres … */): {Resource}
    {
        return $this->{resources}->create(['name' => $name]);
    }
}
```

Fichiers à créer : `Create{Resource}UseCase`, `Update{Resource}UseCase`, `Delete{Resource}UseCase`, `List{Resource}sUseCase`.

Règles :
- Les exceptions métier lèvent `RuntimeException` avec un message traduit.
- Le Use Case ne connaît pas la requête HTTP — il reçoit des scalaires ou des modèles.

---

## 5. Contrôleur (`app/Http/Controllers/Admin/{Resource}ManagementController.php`)

Structure obligatoire — **mince**, délègue tout aux Use Cases :

```php
namespace App\Http\Controllers\Admin;

use App\Http\Controllers\Controller;
use App\UseCases\{Resource}\Create{Resource}UseCase;
use App\UseCases\{Resource}\Delete{Resource}UseCase;
use App\UseCases\{Resource}\List{Resource}sUseCase;
use App\UseCases\{Resource}\Update{Resource}UseCase;
use App\Models\{Resource};
use Illuminate\Http\RedirectResponse;
use Illuminate\Http\Request;
use Inertia\Inertia;
use Inertia\Response;
use RuntimeException;

class {Resource}ManagementController extends Controller
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly List{Resource}sUseCase $list,
        private readonly Create{Resource}UseCase $create,
        private readonly Update{Resource}UseCase $update,
        private readonly Delete{Resource}UseCase $delete,
    ) {}

    public function index(): Response
    {
        return Inertia::render('Admin/{Resources}/Index', [
            'items' => $this->list->execute(),
        ]);
    }

    public function store(Request $request): RedirectResponse
    {
        $validated = $request->validate([/* règles */]);
        $this->create->execute(...$validated);
        return redirect()->route('admin.{resources}.index')->with('success', __('{Resource} créé.'));
    }

    public function update(Request $request, {Resource} ${resource}): RedirectResponse
    {
        $validated = $request->validate([/* règles */]);
        try {
            $this->update->execute(${resource}, $validated);
        } catch (RuntimeException $e) {
            return redirect()->route('admin.{resources}.index')->with('error', $e->getMessage());
        }
        return redirect()->route('admin.{resources}.index')->with('success', __('{Resource} mis à jour.'));
    }

    public function destroy({Resource} ${resource}): RedirectResponse
    {
        try {
            $this->delete->execute(${resource});
        } catch (RuntimeException $e) {
            return redirect()->route('admin.{resources}.index')->with('error', $e->getMessage());
        }
        return redirect()->route('admin.{resources}.index')->with('success', __('{Resource} supprimé.'));
    }
}
```

Règles :
- Redirections toujours vers `admin.{resources}.index` avec `->with('success'|'error', ...)`.
- Validation inline dans le contrôleur.
- Les RuntimeException du Use Case sont capturées et transformées en flash error.

